<LegalPage
  title="Consumer Feedback · Alliance Mutual Escrow"
  description="How to share feedback with Alliance Mutual Escrow: call, email, or leave a review. Every message reaches a person."
  kicker="We want to hear it"
  heading="Consumer feedback"
>
  <h2>Tell us how it went</h2>
  <p>
    Every file closes in someone's life, and we want to know how ours land. Praise, a suggestion,
    or something that fell short: all of it reaches a person, not a queue.
  </p>

  <h2>Three ways to reach us</h2>
  <p><b>Call.</b> (714) 544-6525 and ask for the officer on your file, or for the escrow manager.</p>
  <p><b>Email.</b> <a href="mailto:info@ameescrow.com" style="color:var(--amber)">info@ameescrow.com</a>. Include your escrow number if you have one, and we can pull the file while we read.</p>
  <p><b>Review us.</b> Public reviews help other Californians choose. If we earned a good one, we would be glad to have it. If we did not, tell us first so we can fix what went wrong.</p>

  <h2>What happens with your feedback</h2>
  <p>
    Feedback goes to the escrow manager and is shared with the officer on the file. If something
    needs fixing, our complaint policy explains exactly how that works and what your options are,
    including the state regulator. See the <a href="/complaint-policy" style="color:var(--amber)">complaint policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
